{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LocalOnly collections are designed for in-memory client data or UI state that doesn't need to persist across browser sessions or sync across tabs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localOnlyCollectionOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" allows you to create collections that:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store data only in memory (no persistence)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Support optimistic updates with automatic rollback on errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide optional initial data"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work perfectly for temporary UI state and session-only data"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatically manage the transition from optimistic to confirmed state"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LocalOnly collections are included in the core TanStack DB package:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/react-db","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCollection } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst uiStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'ui-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"direct-local-mutations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct Local Mutations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" LocalOnly collections work differently than server-synced collections. With LocalOnly collections, you "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"directly mutate state"}]},{"type":"text","value":" by calling methods like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.insert()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.update()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.delete()"},{"type":"text","value":" — that's all you need to do. The changes are immediately applied to your local in-memory data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is different from collections that sync with a server (like Query Collection), where mutation handlers send data to a backend. With LocalOnly collections, everything stays local:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Just call the methods directly - no server sync involved\nuiStateCollection.insert({ id: 'theme', mode: 'dark' })\nuiStateCollection.update('theme', (draft) => { draft.mode = 'light' })\nuiStateCollection.delete('theme')","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localOnlyCollectionOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts the following options:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"required-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required Options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":": Unique identifier for the collection"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getKey"},{"type":"text","value":": Function to extract the unique key from an item"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"optional-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional Options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schema"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"link","href":"https://standardschema.dev","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard Schema"}]},{"type":"text","value":" compatible schema (e.g., Zod, Effect) for client-side validation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"},{"type":"text","value":": Array of items to populate the collection with on creation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInsert"},{"type":"text","value":": Optional handler function called before confirming inserts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUpdate"},{"type":"text","value":": Optional handler function called before confirming updates"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDelete"},{"type":"text","value":": Optional handler function called before confirming deletes"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"initial-data","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial Data"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Populate the collection with initial data on creation:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const uiStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'ui-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    initialData: [\n      { id: 'sidebar', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'theme', mode: 'light' },\n      { id: 'modal', visible: false },\n    ],\n  })\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutation-handlers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutation Handlers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutation handlers are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"completely optional"}]},{"type":"text","value":". When provided, they are called before the optimistic state is confirmed:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const tempDataCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'temp-data',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the insert\n      console.log('Inserting:', transaction.mutations[0].modified)\n    },\n    onUpdate: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the update\n      const { original, modified } = transaction.mutations[0]\n      console.log('Updating from', original, 'to', modified)\n    },\n    onDelete: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the delete\n      console.log('Deleting:', transaction.mutations[0].original)\n    },\n  })\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"manual-transactions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual Transactions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using LocalOnly collections with manual transactions (created via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTransaction"},{"type":"text","value":"), you must call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.acceptMutations()"},{"type":"text","value":" to persist the changes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createTransaction } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst localData = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'form-draft',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n\nconst serverCollection = createCollection(\n  queryCollectionOptions({\n    queryKey: ['items'],\n    queryFn: async () => api.items.getAll(),\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      await api.items.create(transaction.mutations[0].modified)\n    },\n  })\n)\n\nconst tx = createTransaction({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    // Handle server collection mutations explicitly in mutationFn\n    await Promise.all(\n      transaction.mutations\n        .filter((m) => m.collection === serverCollection)\n        .map((m) => api.items.create(m.modified))\n    )\n\n    // After server mutations succeed, accept local collection mutations\n    localData.utils.acceptMutations(transaction)\n  },\n})\n\n// Apply mutations to both collections in one transaction\ntx.mutate(() => {\n  localData.insert({ id: 'draft-1', data: '...' })\n  serverCollection.insert({ id: '1', name: 'Item' })\n})\n\nawait tx.commit()","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"complete-example-modal-state-management","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete Example: Modal State Management"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCollection, eq } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { useLiveQuery } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n// Define schema\nconst modalStateSchema = z.object({\n  id: z.string(),\n  isOpen: z.boolean(),\n  data: z.any().optional(),\n})\n\ntype ModalState = z.infer<typeof modalStateSchema>\n\n// Create collection\nexport const modalStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'modal-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    schema: modalStateSchema,\n    initialData: [\n      { id: 'user-profile', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'settings', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'confirm-delete', isOpen: false },\n    ],\n  })\n)\n\n// Use in component\nfunction UserProfileModal() {\n  const { data: modals } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ modal: modalStateCollection })\n        .where(({ modal }) => eq(modal.id, 'user-profile')),\n  })\n\n  const modalState = modals[0]\n\n  const openModal = (data?: any) => {\n    modalStateCollection.update('user-profile', (draft) => {\n      draft.isOpen = true\n      draft.data = data\n    })\n  }\n\n  const closeModal = () => {\n    modalStateCollection.update('user-profile', (draft) => {\n      draft.isOpen = false\n      draft.data = undefined\n    })\n  }\n\n  if (!modalState?.isOpen) return null\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"modal\">\n      <h2>User Profile</h2>\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(modalState.data, null, 2)}</pre>\n      <button onClick={closeModal}>Close</button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"complete-example-form-draft-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete Example: Form Draft State"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCollection, eq } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { useLiveQuery } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\ntype FormDraft = {\n  id: string\n  formData: Record<string, any>\n  lastModified: Date\n}\n\n// Create collection for form drafts\nexport const formDraftsCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'form-drafts',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n\n// Use in component\nfunction CreatePostForm() {\n  const { data: drafts } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ draft: formDraftsCollection })\n        .where(({ draft }) => eq(draft.id, 'new-post')),\n  })\n\n  const currentDraft = drafts[0]\n\n  const updateDraft = (field: string, value: any) => {\n    if (currentDraft) {\n      formDraftsCollection.update('new-post', (draft) => {\n        draft.formData[field] = value\n        draft.lastModified = new Date()\n      })\n    } else {\n      formDraftsCollection.insert({\n        id: 'new-post',\n        formData: { [field]: value },\n        lastModified: new Date(),\n      })\n    }\n  }\n\n  const clearDraft = () => {\n    if (currentDraft) {\n      formDraftsCollection.delete('new-post')\n    }\n  }\n\n  const submitForm = async () => {\n    if (!currentDraft) return\n\n    await api.posts.create(currentDraft.formData)\n    clearDraft()\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); submitForm() }}>\n      <input\n        value={currentDraft?.formData.title || ''}\n        onChange={(e) => updateDraft('title', e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Publish</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={clearDraft}>Clear Draft</button>\n    </form>\n  )\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"use-cases","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Cases"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LocalOnly collections are perfect for:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporary UI state (modals, sidebars, tooltips)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form draft data during the current session"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-side computed or derived data"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wizard/multi-step form state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporary filters or search state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In-memory caches"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"comparison-with-localstoragecollection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison with LocalStorageCollection"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LocalOnly"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LocalStorage"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None (in-memory only)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"localStorage"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cross-tab sync"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Survives page reload"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fastest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fast"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Size limits"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory limits"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"~5-10MB"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best for"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporary UI state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User preferences"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"learn-more","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn More"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./indexed-db-collection.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"IndexedDB Collection"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../guides/mutations.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimistic Mutations"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../guides/live-queries.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live Queries"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./local-storage-collection.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LocalStorage Collection"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"direct-local-mutations","text":"Direct Local Mutations","level":3},{"id":"configuration-options","text":"Configuration Options","level":2},{"id":"required-options","text":"Required Options","level":3},{"id":"optional-options","text":"Optional Options","level":3},{"id":"initial-data","text":"Initial Data","level":2},{"id":"mutation-handlers","text":"Mutation Handlers","level":2},{"id":"manual-transactions","text":"Manual Transactions","level":2},{"id":"complete-example-modal-state-management","text":"Complete Example: Modal State Management","level":2},{"id":"complete-example-form-draft-state","text":"Complete Example: Form Draft State","level":2},{"id":"use-cases","text":"Use Cases","level":2},{"id":"comparison-with-localstoragecollection","text":"Comparison with LocalStorageCollection","level":2},{"id":"learn-more","text":"Learn More","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nLocalOnly collections are designed for in-memory client data or UI state that doesn't need to persist across browser sessions or sync across tabs.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe `localOnlyCollectionOptions` allows you to create collections that:\n- Store data only in memory (no persistence)\n- Support optimistic updates with automatic rollback on errors\n- Provide optional initial data\n- Work perfectly for temporary UI state and session-only data\n- Automatically manage the transition from optimistic to confirmed state\n\n## Installation\n\nLocalOnly collections are included in the core TanStack DB package:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/react-db\n```\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst uiStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'ui-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### Direct Local Mutations\n\n**Important:** LocalOnly collections work differently than server-synced collections. With LocalOnly collections, you **directly mutate state** by calling methods like `collection.insert()`, `collection.update()`, and `collection.delete()` — that's all you need to do. The changes are immediately applied to your local in-memory data.\n\nThis is different from collections that sync with a server (like Query Collection), where mutation handlers send data to a backend. With LocalOnly collections, everything stays local:\n\n```typescript\n// Just call the methods directly - no server sync involved\nuiStateCollection.insert({ id: 'theme', mode: 'dark' })\nuiStateCollection.update('theme', (draft) => { draft.mode = 'light' })\nuiStateCollection.delete('theme')\n```\n\n## Configuration Options\n\nThe `localOnlyCollectionOptions` function accepts the following options:\n\n### Required Options\n\n- `id`: Unique identifier for the collection\n- `getKey`: Function to extract the unique key from an item\n\n### Optional Options\n\n- `schema`: [Standard Schema](https://standardschema.dev) compatible schema (e.g., Zod, Effect) for client-side validation\n- `initialData`: Array of items to populate the collection with on creation\n- `onInsert`: Optional handler function called before confirming inserts\n- `onUpdate`: Optional handler function called before confirming updates\n- `onDelete`: Optional handler function called before confirming deletes\n\n## Initial Data\n\nPopulate the collection with initial data on creation:\n\n```typescript\nconst uiStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'ui-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    initialData: [\n      { id: 'sidebar', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'theme', mode: 'light' },\n      { id: 'modal', visible: false },\n    ],\n  })\n)\n```\n\n## Mutation Handlers\n\nMutation handlers are **completely optional**. When provided, they are called before the optimistic state is confirmed:\n\n```typescript\nconst tempDataCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'temp-data',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the insert\n      console.log('Inserting:', transaction.mutations[0].modified)\n    },\n    onUpdate: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the update\n      const { original, modified } = transaction.mutations[0]\n      console.log('Updating from', original, 'to', modified)\n    },\n    onDelete: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the delete\n      console.log('Deleting:', transaction.mutations[0].original)\n    },\n  })\n)\n```\n\n## Manual Transactions\n\nWhen using LocalOnly collections with manual transactions (created via `createTransaction`), you must call `utils.acceptMutations()` to persist the changes:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createTransaction } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst localData = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'form-draft',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n\nconst serverCollection = createCollection(\n  queryCollectionOptions({\n    queryKey: ['items'],\n    queryFn: async () => api.items.getAll(),\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      await api.items.create(transaction.mutations[0].modified)\n    },\n  })\n)\n\nconst tx = createTransaction({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    // Handle server collection mutations explicitly in mutationFn\n    await Promise.all(\n      transaction.mutations\n        .filter((m) => m.collection === serverCollection)\n        .map((m) => api.items.create(m.modified))\n    )\n\n    // After server mutations succeed, accept local collection mutations\n    localData.utils.acceptMutations(transaction)\n  },\n})\n\n// Apply mutations to both collections in one transaction\ntx.mutate(() => {\n  localData.insert({ id: 'draft-1', data: '...' })\n  serverCollection.insert({ id: '1', name: 'Item' })\n})\n\nawait tx.commit()\n```\n\n## Complete Example: Modal State Management\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection, eq } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { useLiveQuery } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n// Define schema\nconst modalStateSchema = z.object({\n  id: z.string(),\n  isOpen: z.boolean(),\n  data: z.any().optional(),\n})\n\ntype ModalState = z.infer<typeof modalStateSchema>\n\n// Create collection\nexport const modalStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'modal-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    schema: modalStateSchema,\n    initialData: [\n      { id: 'user-profile', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'settings', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'confirm-delete', isOpen: false },\n    ],\n  })\n)\n\n// Use in component\nfunction UserProfileModal() {\n  const { data: modals } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ modal: modalStateCollection })\n        .where(({ modal }) => eq(modal.id, 'user-profile')),\n  })\n\n  const modalState = modals[0]\n\n  const openModal = (data?: any) => {\n    modalStateCollection.update('user-profile', (draft) => {\n      draft.isOpen = true\n      draft.data = data\n    })\n  }\n\n  const closeModal = () => {\n    modalStateCollection.update('user-profile', (draft) => {\n      draft.isOpen = false\n      draft.data = undefined\n    })\n  }\n\n  if (!modalState?.isOpen) return null\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"modal\">\n      <h2>User Profile</h2>\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(modalState.data, null, 2)}</pre>\n      <button onClick={closeModal}>Close</button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Complete Example: Form Draft State\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection, eq } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { useLiveQuery } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\ntype FormDraft = {\n  id: string\n  formData: Record<string, any>\n  lastModified: Date\n}\n\n// Create collection for form drafts\nexport const formDraftsCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'form-drafts',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n\n// Use in component\nfunction CreatePostForm() {\n  const { data: drafts } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ draft: formDraftsCollection })\n        .where(({ draft }) => eq(draft.id, 'new-post')),\n  })\n\n  const currentDraft = drafts[0]\n\n  const updateDraft = (field: string, value: any) => {\n    if (currentDraft) {\n      formDraftsCollection.update('new-post', (draft) => {\n        draft.formData[field] = value\n        draft.lastModified = new Date()\n      })\n    } else {\n      formDraftsCollection.insert({\n        id: 'new-post',\n        formData: { [field]: value },\n        lastModified: new Date(),\n      })\n    }\n  }\n\n  const clearDraft = () => {\n    if (currentDraft) {\n      formDraftsCollection.delete('new-post')\n    }\n  }\n\n  const submitForm = async () => {\n    if (!currentDraft) return\n\n    await api.posts.create(currentDraft.formData)\n    clearDraft()\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); submitForm() }}>\n      <input\n        value={currentDraft?.formData.title || ''}\n        onChange={(e) => updateDraft('title', e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Publish</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={clearDraft}>Clear Draft</button>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Use Cases\n\nLocalOnly collections are perfect for:\n- Temporary UI state (modals, sidebars, tooltips)\n- Form draft data during the current session\n- Client-side computed or derived data\n- Wizard/multi-step form state\n- Temporary filters or search state\n- In-memory caches\n\n## Comparison with LocalStorageCollection\n\n| Feature | LocalOnly | LocalStorage |\n|---------|-----------|--------------|\n| Persistence | None (in-memory only) | localStorage |\n| Cross-tab sync | No | Yes |\n| Survives page reload | No | Yes |\n| Performance | Fastest | Fast |\n| Size limits | Memory limits | ~5-10MB |\n| Best for | Temporary UI state | User preferences |\n\n## Learn More\n\n- [IndexedDB Collection](./indexed-db-collection.md)\n\n- [Optimistic Mutations](../guides/mutations.md)\n- [Live Queries](../guides/live-queries.md)\n- [LocalStorage Collection](./local-storage-collection.md)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: LocalOnly Collection\n---\n\nLocalOnly collections are designed for in-memory client data or UI state that doesn't need to persist across browser sessions or sync across tabs.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe `localOnlyCollectionOptions` allows you to create collections that:\n- Store data only in memory (no persistence)\n- Support optimistic updates with automatic rollback on errors\n- Provide optional initial data\n- Work perfectly for temporary UI state and session-only data\n- Automatically manage the transition from optimistic to confirmed state\n\n## Installation\n\nLocalOnly collections are included in the core TanStack DB package:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/react-db\n```\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst uiStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'ui-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### Direct Local Mutations\n\n**Important:** LocalOnly collections work differently than server-synced collections. With LocalOnly collections, you **directly mutate state** by calling methods like `collection.insert()`, `collection.update()`, and `collection.delete()` — that's all you need to do. The changes are immediately applied to your local in-memory data.\n\nThis is different from collections that sync with a server (like Query Collection), where mutation handlers send data to a backend. With LocalOnly collections, everything stays local:\n\n```typescript\n// Just call the methods directly - no server sync involved\nuiStateCollection.insert({ id: 'theme', mode: 'dark' })\nuiStateCollection.update('theme', (draft) => { draft.mode = 'light' })\nuiStateCollection.delete('theme')\n```\n\n## Configuration Options\n\nThe `localOnlyCollectionOptions` function accepts the following options:\n\n### Required Options\n\n- `id`: Unique identifier for the collection\n- `getKey`: Function to extract the unique key from an item\n\n### Optional Options\n\n- `schema`: [Standard Schema](https://standardschema.dev) compatible schema (e.g., Zod, Effect) for client-side validation\n- `initialData`: Array of items to populate the collection with on creation\n- `onInsert`: Optional handler function called before confirming inserts\n- `onUpdate`: Optional handler function called before confirming updates\n- `onDelete`: Optional handler function called before confirming deletes\n\n## Initial Data\n\nPopulate the collection with initial data on creation:\n\n```typescript\nconst uiStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'ui-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    initialData: [\n      { id: 'sidebar', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'theme', mode: 'light' },\n      { id: 'modal', visible: false },\n    ],\n  })\n)\n```\n\n## Mutation Handlers\n\nMutation handlers are **completely optional**. When provided, they are called before the optimistic state is confirmed:\n\n```typescript\nconst tempDataCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'temp-data',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the insert\n      console.log('Inserting:', transaction.mutations[0].modified)\n    },\n    onUpdate: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the update\n      const { original, modified } = transaction.mutations[0]\n      console.log('Updating from', original, 'to', modified)\n    },\n    onDelete: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      // Custom logic before confirming the delete\n      console.log('Deleting:', transaction.mutations[0].original)\n    },\n  })\n)\n```\n\n## Manual Transactions\n\nWhen using LocalOnly collections with manual transactions (created via `createTransaction`), you must call `utils.acceptMutations()` to persist the changes:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createTransaction } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst localData = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'form-draft',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n\nconst serverCollection = createCollection(\n  queryCollectionOptions({\n    queryKey: ['items'],\n    queryFn: async () => api.items.getAll(),\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      await api.items.create(transaction.mutations[0].modified)\n    },\n  })\n)\n\nconst tx = createTransaction({\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    // Handle server collection mutations explicitly in mutationFn\n    await Promise.all(\n      transaction.mutations\n        .filter((m) => m.collection === serverCollection)\n        .map((m) => api.items.create(m.modified))\n    )\n\n    // After server mutations succeed, accept local collection mutations\n    localData.utils.acceptMutations(transaction)\n  },\n})\n\n// Apply mutations to both collections in one transaction\ntx.mutate(() => {\n  localData.insert({ id: 'draft-1', data: '...' })\n  serverCollection.insert({ id: '1', name: 'Item' })\n})\n\nawait tx.commit()\n```\n\n## Complete Example: Modal State Management\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection, eq } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { useLiveQuery } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n// Define schema\nconst modalStateSchema = z.object({\n  id: z.string(),\n  isOpen: z.boolean(),\n  data: z.any().optional(),\n})\n\ntype ModalState = z.infer<typeof modalStateSchema>\n\n// Create collection\nexport const modalStateCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'modal-state',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    schema: modalStateSchema,\n    initialData: [\n      { id: 'user-profile', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'settings', isOpen: false },\n      { id: 'confirm-delete', isOpen: false },\n    ],\n  })\n)\n\n// Use in component\nfunction UserProfileModal() {\n  const { data: modals } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ modal: modalStateCollection })\n        .where(({ modal }) => eq(modal.id, 'user-profile')),\n  })\n\n  const modalState = modals[0]\n\n  const openModal = (data?: any) => {\n    modalStateCollection.update('user-profile', (draft) => {\n      draft.isOpen = true\n      draft.data = data\n    })\n  }\n\n  const closeModal = () => {\n    modalStateCollection.update('user-profile', (draft) => {\n      draft.isOpen = false\n      draft.data = undefined\n    })\n  }\n\n  if (!modalState?.isOpen) return null\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"modal\">\n      <h2>User Profile</h2>\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(modalState.data, null, 2)}</pre>\n      <button onClick={closeModal}>Close</button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Complete Example: Form Draft State\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection, eq } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { localOnlyCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { useLiveQuery } from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\ntype FormDraft = {\n  id: string\n  formData: Record<string, any>\n  lastModified: Date\n}\n\n// Create collection for form drafts\nexport const formDraftsCollection = createCollection(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'form-drafts',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n\n// Use in component\nfunction CreatePostForm() {\n  const { data: drafts } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ draft: formDraftsCollection })\n        .where(({ draft }) => eq(draft.id, 'new-post')),\n  })\n\n  const currentDraft = drafts[0]\n\n  const updateDraft = (field: string, value: any) => {\n    if (currentDraft) {\n      formDraftsCollection.update('new-post', (draft) => {\n        draft.formData[field] = value\n        draft.lastModified = new Date()\n      })\n    } else {\n      formDraftsCollection.insert({\n        id: 'new-post',\n        formData: { [field]: value },\n        lastModified: new Date(),\n      })\n    }\n  }\n\n  const clearDraft = () => {\n    if (currentDraft) {\n      formDraftsCollection.delete('new-post')\n    }\n  }\n\n  const submitForm = async () => {\n    if (!currentDraft) return\n\n    await api.posts.create(currentDraft.formData)\n    clearDraft()\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); submitForm() }}>\n      <input\n        value={currentDraft?.formData.title || ''}\n        onChange={(e) => updateDraft('title', e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\">Publish</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" onClick={clearDraft}>Clear Draft</button>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Use Cases\n\nLocalOnly collections are perfect for:\n- Temporary UI state (modals, sidebars, tooltips)\n- Form draft data during the current session\n- Client-side computed or derived data\n- Wizard/multi-step form state\n- Temporary filters or search state\n- In-memory caches\n\n## Comparison with LocalStorageCollection\n\n| Feature | LocalOnly | LocalStorage |\n|---------|-----------|--------------|\n| Persistence | None (in-memory only) | localStorage |\n| Cross-tab sync | No | Yes |\n| Survives page reload | No | Yes |\n| Performance | Fastest | Fast |\n| Size limits | Memory limits | ~5-10MB |\n| Best for | Temporary UI state | User preferences |\n\n## Learn More\n\n- [IndexedDB Collection](./indexed-db-collection.md)\n\n- [Optimistic Mutations](../guides/mutations.md)\n- [Live Queries](../guides/live-queries.md)\n- [LocalStorage Collection](./local-storage-collection.md)\n"}
